cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Microchip Oil Segmentation: automated quantification of oil recovery in
  microfluidic EOR experiments
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the paper
  whose analysis it produced.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Omar
    family-names: Choudhry
    affiliation: School of Computing, University of Leeds
    website: 'https://omarchoudhry.co.uk'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/omariosc/microchips'
url: 'https://github.com/omariosc/microchips'
abstract: >-
  Computer-vision software for quantifying oil distribution in microfluidic
  micromodel flooding experiments. Oil is segmented from time-lapse transmitted
  light micrographs by k-means dominant-colour extraction followed by Euclidean
  colour-distance thresholding, morphological opening and connected-component
  area filtering. Per-frame oil area ratios are converted into tertiary oil
  recovery curves and fitted with an exponential decay model. Written for the
  micromodel flooding tests reported in Tliba et al. (2025), Journal of
  Molecular Liquids.
keywords:
  - image segmentation
  - computer vision
  - opencv
  - microfluidics
  - enhanced oil recovery
  - micromodel
  - porous media
  - scientific image analysis
license: MIT
year: 2025
